%I A402746 #13 Nov 27 2026 16:58:00
%S A402746 6944085556321,6944085556327,6944085556361,6944085556367,
%T A402746 6944085556393,6944085556487,6944085556543,6944085556579,
%U A402746 6944085556649,6944085556657,6944085557677,6944085557681,6944085557707,6944085558001,6944085558023,6944085558041,6944085558043,6944085558121
%N A402746 Primes p for which pi_{120;13,37,83,107}(p) - pi_{120;1,49,71,119}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A402746 This sequence is about one of the 105 prime races modulo 120 between cosets of index 8 in (Z/120Z)* containing (Z/120Z)*^2; see A401958 for more details. Specifically, here we have H = {1,49,71,119} and S = {13,37,83,107}, corresponding to T = {chi_5, chi_8, chi_24, chi_60}, where chi_d = (d/.) is the Kronecker symbol viewed as a character modulo N = 120. Note that (Z/120Z)*^2 = {1,49}, and {71,119}, {13,37}, {83,107} are cosets of it in (Z/120Z)*.
%C A402746 Assuming GRH and LI, the set of x with pi_{120;13,37,83,107}(x) > pi_{120;1,49,71,119}(x) has logarithmic density 0.99870, making the race between {1,49,71,119} and {13,37,83,107} the 25th most biased among the 105 races between cosets of index 8 in (Z/120Z)*; see the Zenodo preprint "Logarithmic densities of prime number races between the cosets of subgroups containing the squares modulo 120" below.
%C A402746 Let D(x) = pi_{120;13,37,83,107}(x) - pi_{120;1,49,71,119}(x). (We have D(x0) = 21067 for x0 = 7*10^12; for the concrete numbers of primes below x0 in each congruence class modulo 120, see the file "pi_mod120_at_7e12.csv" in the Zenodo preprint). There is only one sign-changing zone giving a total of 15378 terms below x0:
%C A402746   a(1..15378) = 6944085556321-6944583992149 (there are 14991315 primes a(1) <= p <= a(15378) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -1216 at p = 6944426887441).
%H A402746 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402746/b402746.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..15378</a> (all terms below 7*10^12)
%H A402746 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24516487">Logarithmic densities of prime number races between the cosets of subgroups containing the squares modulo 120</a>, preprint, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A402746 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A402746 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A402746 Andrey S. Shchebetov, <a href="https://math101.guru/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/01-A3-Presentation-v7.3EN-no.pdf">Testing Chebyshev's bias for prime numbers up to 10^15</a>, EUCYS 2018.
%H A402746 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A402746 (PARI) my(k=0, r=0); forprime(p=6944085556321, 7e12, r=p%120; if(r==1||r==49||r==71||r==119, k--); if(r==13||r==37||r==83||r==107, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A402746 Cf. Races between cosets of index 8 in (Z/120Z)*: A298821 (11th), A297450 (19th), A402745 (21st), A295356 (23rd), this sequence (25th).
%Y A402746 See A401958 for races between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*.
%K A402746 nonn,new
%O A402746 1,1
%A A402746 _Leandro Hector Gallego_ and _Jianing Song_, Nov 26 2026
